      "caption": {
        "body": "In the 1860s, Minton \u0026 Company, a major English ceramic producer whose wares ranged from affordable transferware to hand-decorated porcelain and large-scale monumental design, acquired books of Japanese birds and flowers. “Bamboo \u0026 Fan” is one of several Minton patterns that use the same fan template as a frame for different bird motifs.  See “Japonisme: A Passion for Japan” on display, post-security, in Terminal 2 and online at: https://bit.ly/JaponismeSFO",
